   "abstract": "A 2-bedroom home move of 10 road miles, off peak: $58–$103 with a rental truck before help, $390–$1,380 with a container, and $720–$1,800 with full-service movers. Tip guides suggest $4–$15 per mover per hour: $16–$98 per mover for 4–6.5 hours on site, $48–$294 for 3 movers. Guides put a 2-bedroom home at about 40–90 boxes. A 2-bedroom home move takes up about 640–930 cu ft: the smallest truck that holds the heavy end is 20 ft. With 3 movers, a 2-bedroom home move takes about 4–6.5 hours on site: $720–$1,800 off peak at 10 road miles. The moving checklist has 14 tasks, from 8 weeks before the move to after the move. Each result is a range: the low end fits a light load and easy access, the high end a fuller home or a harder day. Sample figures assume 10 or 1,000 road miles, an off-peak date, no stairs and no extras. Tips, supplies, parking permits and travel sit outside the result, so budget them on top. A written estimate far below the range is a reason to ask questions, not a bargain to grab.",
   "alternateName": "Moving cost calculator for local and long-distance moves",
