    {
     "@id": "https://liftmyboxes.com/moving-cost-calculator/#countdown-checklist-section",
     "@type": "WebPageElement",
     "cssSelector": "#countdown-checklist",
     "description": "A section of the Moving cost calculator page: Keeping the final bill close to the estimate",
     "hasPart": {
      "@id": "https://liftmyboxes.com/moving-cost-calculator/#countdown-checklist-howto",
      "@type": "HowTo",
      "name": "Keeping the final bill close to the estimate",
      "step": [
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": {
         "@type": "HowToStep",
         "name": "List everything that's moving, largest pieces first",
         "position": 1,
         "text": "Give every company the same list, so their estimates price the same job."
        },
        "name": "8 weeks before"
       },
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": {
         "@type": "HowToStep",
         "name": "Ask each building, park or association about its moving rules",
         "position": 1,
         "text": "Moving hours, elevators, loading docks and gates. If one wants the company's certificate of insurance, ask the company to send it ahead."
        },
        "name": "6 weeks before"
       },
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": {
         "@type": "HowToStep",
         "name": "Ask how and when the company wants to be paid",
         "position": 1,
         "text": "Whether it takes a deposit, when the rest is due, and which payment methods it accepts."
        },
        "name": "4 weeks before"
       },
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": {
         "@type": "HowToStep",
         "name": "Ask who to call if something goes wrong on the day",
         "position": 1,
         "text": "Get a name and a direct number, not only the main office line."
        },
        "name": "2 weeks before"
       },
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": [
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Confirm the date, arrival window and addresses with the company",
          "position": 1,
          "text": "Ask for a phone number that will be answered on moving day."
         },
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Save parking for the truck at both ends",
          "position": 2,
          "text": "Ask the building or the city whether you need a permit or cones."
         }
        ],
        "name": "1 week before"
       },
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": [
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Empty, defrost and dry the fridge and freezer",
          "position": 1,
          "text": "Eat down the frozen food in the weeks before, so little is left to throw away."
         },
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Charge your phone and keep the paperwork with you",
          "position": 2,
          "text": "Have the estimate and the company's number where you can reach them."
         }
        ],
        "name": "The day before"
       },
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": [
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Check each piece as it comes off the truck",
          "position": 1,
          "text": "Note any damage on the paperwork before you sign for delivery."
         },
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Check every room, closet and cabinet before the truck leaves",
          "position": 2,
          "text": "Look high and low: top shelves, under sinks, the attic and the garage."
         },
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Walk the crew lead through what goes and what stays",
          "position": 3,
          "text": "Point out anything fragile, very heavy or going to a particular room."
         },
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Watch the loading and unloading",
          "position": 4,
          "text": "FMCSA's advice: if you can't be there, ask someone you know to act for you."
         }
        ],
        "name": "Moving day"
       },
       {
        "@type": "HowToSection",
        "itemListElement": [
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Set up the beds first",
          "position": 1,
          "text": "Then the kitchen basics; the rest can wait a day."
         },
         {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "name": "Report any damage to the company in writing",
          "position": 2,
          "text": "Send photos and a list of what's damaged or missing as soon as you find it."
         }
        ],
        "name": "After the move"
       }
      ]
     },
     "name": "Keeping the final bill close to the estimate"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://liftmyboxes.com/moving-cost-calculator/#faq",
     "@type": "FAQPage",
     "isPartOf": {
      "@id": "https://liftmyboxes.com/moving-cost-calculator/#webpage"
     },
     "mainEntity": [
      {
       "@type": "Question",
       "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Start with a moving cost calculator: enter both ZIP codes, your home size, the date and any extras to get a range. A studio apartment moved 10 road miles, off peak with no stairs or extras, comes to $280–$740. Then add the costs movers don't charge for, such as tips, supplies and travel, and ask movers for written estimates to firm it up."
       },
       "name": "How do you estimate the cost of a move?"
      },
      {
       "@type": "Question",
       "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It's free, and the range appears on the page without an email or a sign-up. The moving cost calculator takes about a minute: you enter ZIP codes, home size, date and extras, and the price range shows straight away."
       },
       "name": "Is the moving cost calculator free, and does it need an email?"
      },
      {
       "@type": "Question",
       "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "With movers, a 3-bedroom home moved 10 road miles costs $1,150–$2,850, and moved 1,000 road miles it costs $4,000–$8,550, both off peak with no stairs or extras. Smaller homes cost less and bigger ones more. Run the moving cost calculator with your own ZIP codes and date for a range that fits your move."
       },
       "name": "How much should I expect to pay to move?"
      },
      {
       "@type": "Question",
       "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For a local move, multiply the crew size by the hourly rate and the hours: one mover typically costs $50–$75 an hour, truck included, so a 3-mover crew costs three times that. For a long move, the sum uses the weight of the shipment and the miles instead. A moving cost calculator does both sums from your inputs, and gives a range rather than one average figure."
       },
       "name": "How is an average moving cost calculated?"
      },
      {
       "@type": "Question",
       "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Not directly. The moving cost calculator asks for your home size and uses that as a stand-in for weight. Movers weigh a long-distance shipment, or estimate it after a survey, so their figure can differ if your rooms are fuller or emptier than most. Tell each mover about heavy pieces, such as a gun safe or a piano, at the survey."
       },
       "name": "Can a moving cost calculator price a move by weight?"
      }
     ],
     "name": "Moving cost calculator FAQ",
     "url": "https://liftmyboxes.com/moving-cost-calculator/"
    }
   ],
